{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210078,"nonce":"oPIRBxZ41+51cTjrrMTAMDpQKJ0=","title":"a field read on a Null\u003canon\u003e receiver types as Dynamic; the fix exposes a closure crash in haxe.Template","message":"TWO LINKED FACTS, both measured.\n\n1. THE GAP. In compiler/src/tast/ast_lowering/infer.rs, the field-type walk\nfor `TypedExpressionKind::FieldAccess` follows TypeAlias and Class but not\n`Optional`. So for `t = l.first()` (typed `Null\u003c{p:String,s:Bool}\u003e`), `t.p`\ninfers as Dynamic. Uncaptured this is mostly hidden (the MIR register type\ncarries the day); once the local is CAPTURED it takes the Dynamic path:\n\n    var p = t.p;\n    function inner() return p.length;   // p captured -\u003e Dynamic cell\n    p.length                            // rayzor_anon_get_field_by_index slot 3 on\n                                        // haxe_unbox_reference_ptr(cell): SIGSEGV 0x22\n\n/tmp/probe/CAPP2.hx: literal captured OK, plain-anon captured OK,\nlist-anon captured CRASH. It is also the cause of 5198295 (`lt.first().p ==\n\"rr\"` false): the == compared a Dynamic.\n\n2. THE FIX WORKS AND BREAKS TEMPLATE. Adding an `Optional { inner_type }` arm\nthat continues the walk into the inner type fixes CAPP2 (all four cases) AND\n5198295 (all four cases true). But with it, haxe.Template templates that use\nan expression -- `::if x::`, `::foreach items::` -- crash in `\u003clambda_haxe__0\u003e`\nwith the fault equal to the NAME string's bytes (`0x7820` = \"x \",\n`0x736d65746920` = \"items \"): a String is being dereferenced as an object\ninside a Template closure (makeConst's `function() return me.resolve(v)`, or\nmakePath's `Reflect.field(e(), f)`). Conformance rows 5293 and 9372 go\nWRONG_ANSWER -\u003e CRASH. Bisected: removing the arm returns them to\nWRONG_ANSWER. The arm is HELD BACK for that reason; the diff is one match arm:\n\n    crate::tast::core::TypeKind::Optional { inner_type } =\u003e {\n        current = *inner_type; hops += 1;\n    }\n\nSo the arm is correct and the crash is a pre-existing closure/capture defect\nthat Dynamic typing was masking. Find what in those closures mis-handles a\nString-typed captured field where it used to get a Dynamic; then land both.","files":null}]}